# Rounded stack on the best measured base (Gate 0 Final #11 S=21.0 + D Val #24).
# Not a promise of S>=90. Cold Finals so far top out at 21.0 because peak TPOT
# stays ~88ms and only ~120/300 requests meet SLO. S>=90 needs ~240/300 and
# p95 TPOT <= 50ms together. This profile only adds unburned levers that attack
# that gap:
#   1. --max-num-active-seqs 80  (D Val: no TTFT cliff, Acc 90.8%; unlike max-num-seqs 64)
#   2. --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16  (smaller hybrid state, more cache room)
#   3. --prefix-match-unit 16  (finer hits inside a large hybrid block; cold Final hit ~44%)
# Held from Gate 0: budget 2048, mem 0.95, APC on, MTP off, no --max-num-seqs, no power cap.
# Do not add: ngram, MTP, budgets 1024/1536/3072/8192, FP8 KV (A100 hybrid).
CMKL/MANGO1.5-Qwen3.5-9B-AWQ-W4A16-mtp
--host 0.0.0.0
--port 8000
--served-model-name mango1.5-awq-w4a16
--trust-remote-code
--gpu-memory-utilization 0.95
--max-model-len 40960
--enable-auto-tool-choice
--tool-call-parser qwen3_coder
--reasoning-parser qwen3
--enable-chunked-prefill
--max-num-batched-tokens 2048
--max-num-active-seqs 80
--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16
--prefix-match-unit 16
--enable-prefix-caching
# --mamba-cache-mode align matches run5/profile.args.
# On vLLM 0.32.1rc1.dev361+g83c078d95, --mamba-cache-mode is deprecated and has no effect.
# Mamba prefix caching follows --enable-prefix-caching.
# flag-check may WARN that "align" is absent from that deprecation text. That WARN is expected.
--mamba-cache-mode align
